replies-view.ts`). A held draft never projects an affordance of its own (invariant #4 as structure): `none`×held and `posted`×held project `row_action 'none'` — a posted row keeps its live Google reply visible and silently withdraws Regenerate — while `orphan`×held keeps `recover`, because recovery addresses the orphan incident, not the draft. The `held` value itself never reaches the browser: the card reconstructs the "Reply on hold" panel for an unanswered held row from `reply_state 'none'` + `row_action 'none'`. The `gap` / `historical` section split derived from `subscription_activated_at` is deleted here, surviving only as a per-row `ProvenanceBadge` (`posted_before_joining` / `replied_on_google` / `auto_approved` / `owner_approved`); `PAST_REPLIES_VIEW_ENABLED` was **retired with it at #678** — the list renders unconditionally — while `EDIT_REPLIES_ENABLED` is kept (it gates the live-Google mutation) and `editRepliesEnabled()` (`src/lib/past-replies/flags.ts`) is now its only reader. _Avoid_: Past Replies, the archive, History tab (all name the pre-#671 surface), All Reviews page (it is a tab, not a page). *(coined in #671; spec §6.3a, §6.4; implemented at #678; remodelled at #727 per #723)*
