    36	## Capacity & scale (locked 2026-07-16 — wayfinder map #472)
    37	
    38	- **Capacity target**: the load production is deliberately sized for — 250 locations at 6 months, ~125 reviews/day steady, a 1000-event/10-minute ingest burst drained within 30 minutes, peak 10 concurrent dashboard renders. Owned by ticket #474's resolution; ADR 0005 addendum mirrors it. Sizing beyond it requires re-opening the ticket, not silently raising numbers.
    39	- **Design burst**: the worst-case ingest spike the pipeline must absorb without data loss — a multi-day Zernio webhook replay plus ~6 simultaneous onboardings (per-location onboarding cost is bounded by the consented Review import: ≤100 reviews inside the Import window since #675; was "backfill capped ~50" pre-#675 — same order of magnitude, burst sizing unchanged).
    40	- **Summed LLM worker-slot cap**: the de facto global LLM concurrency limit on a single-replica worker — the sum of BullMQ `concurrency` across all non-flag-gated LLM-calling queues (≤**9**; boot-enforced by `assertSummedLlmWorkerSlots`, `worker/config/startup-assert.ts`). Flag-gated `judge_verdict` is capped at 1 separately, outside the sum. Worker *slots*, not provider calls: per-job fan-out (the demo lane's `Promise.allSettled`, ≤15 reviews) is a sanctioned unguarded lane bounded by its review-count cap and admin rate limits. Exceeding ~10 is a named trigger that forces building a global Redis semaphore first (ADR 0005 addendum). *(was "Summed LLM concurrency cap (≤8)" — #490's inventory missed `generate_demo`; renamed and corrected to the true sum, 2026-07-20)*
    41	- **LLM provider circuit breaker**: an in-process, per-provider (`LLMProviderId`) breaker in the `src/lib/llm/` seam, consulted by `runLlmTask`. States closed/open/half-open; trips after **5** consecutive `isTransientLLMError` failures, stays **open 30s**, then admits **one** half-open probe (success or a non-transient response closes it; a transient probe failure re-opens). Open primary ⇒ skip its ~30s timeout and fail over to the fallback provider; **any provider blocked ⇒ retryable `TransientLLMError`** (never a terminal loss), terminal only when every provider was attempted and every attempt non-transient. Trip (closed→open) and recovery (→closed) emit a Sentry `warning`; other real transitions (open↔half_open churn) are structured-log-only (deviations D4). In-process ⇒ effectively global only under single-replica (ADR 0005), same posture as the Summed LLM worker-slot cap; multi-replica defers to the same Redis-semaphore trigger. Gated by `LLM_CIRCUIT_BREAKER_ENABLED` (default ON; only `false` disables). *(coined in ticket F3/P9, 2026-07-20)*
    42	- **Backlog depth**: the count of `status='pending'` rows in a dispatch-queue table (`job_outbox`, `analytics_events`) — **total** pending, including not-yet-due retry rows (NOT "claimable only"; no `available_at <= NOW()` filter). A saturation signal against the Capacity target. Single owner: `queryBacklogDepth(sql)` (`src/lib/shared/backlog-depth.ts`), read by both the `/internal/queue-health` endpoint and the HealthAlertPoller. *(coined in the #472 observability effort, ticket #480)*
    43	- **Backlog depth alert threshold**: the per-table pending-row count (`HEALTH_ALERT_BACKLOG_DEPTH_THRESHOLD`, default **1500**, sized to the #474 Capacity target) above which HealthAlertPoller emits a `warning` (`backlog_depth:<table>`) — a saturation nudge, not dropped work; the 5s OutboxPoller drain normally clears it. *(coined in the #472 observability effort, ticket #480)*
    44	- **Health-bundle differential**: the checked-in `scripts/health-bundle-differential.ts` experiment (ticket #505) that isolates concurrent-`Promise.all`-vs-sequential × pool-size (`max:2` vs `max:6`) on the REAL health-check query mix (the shipped `checkXxx`/`runHealthChecks` from `worker/background/pollers/health-alert/checks.ts`), reusing the exact resolved health config so the queries fired are identical to production. Three arms — `concurrent-max2` (expect **wedged**), `sequential-max2` (the shipped cure, expect clean), `concurrent-max6` (pool-size control, expect clean) — proving the pipelining Connection wedge is pool-size×mix, not concurrency alone. Runs against an **ephemeral Supabase branch** off staging where it is the sole client, so cleanup (terminate every wedge-signature backend) needs no per-backend attribution and cannot contaminate shared staging or the #507 soak. *(coined in the #505 differential + burst-drill effort)*
    45	- **Capacity-burst drill**: the two-arm operational drill (ticket #505/#480) driven by the checked-in `scripts/burst-drill-load.ts` against shared staging, proving outbox DISPATCH-drain of a burst of pending `job_outbox` rows plus Backlog depth observability — **not** full ingest→draft→notification (LLM) pipeline throughput. **Headroom arm**: ~1000 immediately-claimable rows paced over 10 minutes; drain rate (~600/min) outpaces injection, backlog stays low, drains ≤30 min, and `backlog_depth:job_outbox` does **not** fire — proves drain + no false alarm. **Over-threshold arm**: ~1600 future-dated rows that count toward Backlog depth but the poller cannot yet claim, so pending holds above the Backlog depth alert threshold across a poller tick and `backlog_depth:job_outbox` fires; a scoped `release` then clears the injected rows and the alert clears (pending drops below threshold **and** a subsequent HealthAlertPoller cycle completes a clean check-in emitting no such finding — `emit.ts` has no separate recovery event). *(coined in the #505 differential + burst-drill effort)*
