    56	## Solicitation (send-mode) — locked 2026-07-28 (ticket #619, wayfinder map #617)
    57	
    58	Extends the watch-mode entries above; it never replaces them. Watch-mode reserved
    59	**Outreach** for send-mode's actual sends and deferred the batch `expired` state to
    60	send-mode — both land here.
    61	
    62	- **Outreach row**: one `solicitation_outreach` row — one dispatch attempt for one **Ask**, carrying the rendered subject/body and the send lifecycle (`delivery_status` over `rendered | queued | sending | sent | withheld | cancelled | failed | unknown`, with a `disposition_reason` on every reason-bearing status and none on `rendered`/`queued`/`sending`/`sent`). This is the send-mode sense watch-mode reserved the word for: the ask says what the restraint policy decided and never changes (090 welded its status to `evidence->>'decision'`), the outreach row says what happened. One live attempt per ask (partial unique over `rendered`/`queued`/`sending`) and attempt numbers are never reused (`UNIQUE (ask_id, attempt_no)`); a regenerate terminalizes the prior row `cancelled`/`superseded` and inserts `attempt_no + 1` in the same transaction. _Avoid_: message row, ask message, send record. *(coined in the #619 executor/approval map; table created by migration 091 in #624)*
    63	- **Send batch parent**: the `agent_runs` row of kind `solicitation_send_batch` (`subject_type='solicitation_batch'`) — the sequential sibling of watch-mode's terminal `solicitation_batch` build run. It starts when the send lane engages (generation), spans the approval wait, and terminalizes when the drip closes. Legitimately long-lived but bounded **by construction** at ≤10 days (7-day approval window + 72-hour send window), which is exactly why the spine's `stalled` threshold became kind-aware rather than raised by feel. _Avoid_: send run, drip run. *(coined in #619 D3; ADR 0014)*
    64	- **Lazy child**: a per-dispatch-attempt `solicitation_ask` child run created **at release**, not at build — the send-mode counterpart of watch-mode's **Logical fan-out**. Children live minutes (consent recheck → dispatch → provider result → terminal), so no run is ever long-lived enough to be misread as `stalled`, the **Halt latch** has nothing to cancel in the spine, and the join needs no pre-enumeration of children. The plan stays in `solicitation_asks`; the spine records work *performed*, never work *planned* — so the spine deliberately cannot answer "how many children will this batch have." *(coined in #619 D3; ADR 0014)*
    65	- **Settled batch**: a batch with no outreach row left in `rendered`, `queued` or `sending` — the join condition, asked of the domain table and never of `agent_runs`. Every writer that terminalizes an **Outreach row** calls `closeBatchIfSettled` in the *same* transaction, so there is no window between terminalizing and joining; it CASes `send_closed_at` on NULL (a second caller writes nothing, not even a duplicate receipt), records one close step, and terminalizes the **Send batch parent** through the disposition lookup (`exhausted`→`completed`; `halted`/`expired`→`cancelled`; `gate_closed`/`generation_failed`→`failed`). The releaser tick is a backstop calling the same function — one implementation, two callers, no join poller. Disposition is an ordered precedence over explicit sources; the status counts are the receipt's *evidence*, not the decision. *(coined in #619 D11/D14; `closeBatchIfSettled` in `src/lib/solicitation/outreach.ts`)*
    66	- **Batch state**: the read-time `deriveBatchState(row, now)` over `solicitation_batches`' monotone timestamps — a closed union with fixed precedence `halted > closed > sending > veto_window > approved > expired > built > pending`. There is deliberately **no `status` column**: it would be a second owner of a fact the timestamps already carry, needing its own transition CHECK to stay honest. **This is where watch-mode's deferred `expired` finally lands.** The **Solicitation batch** entry above records that `expired` was specified but never implemented, because watch-mode had nothing for it to gate; here it gates approval — a batch past its 7-day approval window may not be approved by either lane — and such batches are closed through the **Halt latch** with reason `batch_expired`. `built` is the same fact watch-mode's lifecycle names; watch-mode's `reviewed` is not a member of this union, which derives send-lane facts only. *(coined in #619 D2; ADR 0014)*
    67	- **Body redaction**: the 90-day post-send NULLing of `rendered_subject`/`rendered_body` **and emptying of `interpolation_inputs` to `'{}'`**, with `body_redacted_at` stamped and the metadata row kept forever — data minimization on third-party PII held on the contact's behalf, timed comfortably past the 14-day attribution window and past bounce/complaint feedback lag. The source goes with the prose: `interpolation_inputs` carries `contact_first_name` and `visit_note`, so redacting only the rendered text would delete the sentence and keep its ingredients. This is enforced in the schema, not merely in the sweep — `solicitation_outreach_body_presence` requires `body_redacted_at IS NULL OR interpolation_inputs = '{}'::jsonb`, so no future writer can stamp a redaction and skip the erasure. It costs the post-90-day reproducibility of the `unverifiable_fact` provenance verdict (#623 §2.4), which was already lost at the same instant anyway: that verdict is computed over `subject + body`, both of which this same sweep deletes. It is **not a delete**, which is why the retention inventory carries it as a novel shape (redact-in-place, plus purge-by-cascade). **Redaction implies TERMINAL, and that is one window on two clocks**: a `sent` row ages from `sent_at`, while a row that settled without ever sending (`withheld`/`cancelled`/`failed`/`unknown`) has no `sent_at` and ages from `rendered_at`. A LIVE row (`rendered`/`queued`/`sending`) is never redactable at any age — a bodyless live attempt can neither send nor settle, and wedges its batch behind `solicitation_outreach_one_live_per_ask`, which is the hazard the rule exists for. #624 shipped the rule as "implies **sent**", which made the stamp unrepresentable on the four never-sent terminals and left their bodies and inputs retained forever (#636 / step-7 S2); 092 widened it to the hazard's actual shape. Swept by two bounded arms of the existing `ArchivalPoller` — no new poller, because the single-replica P2 duplicate-processing budget was already spent — each oldest-first with `SKIP LOCKED`, capped at 5000 rows per cycle and logged as saturated at its own cap. A body is never logged. _Avoid_: body purge, body expiry. *(coined in #619 D6b/D6c; swept in #624; completed in #636)*
    68	- **Halt latch**: the single monotone `halted_at`/`halt_reason`/`halted_by` write on `solicitation_batches` that stops a send batch — one mechanism, five reasons (`owner_veto`, `owner_halt`, `admin_halt`, `send_window_elapsed`, `batch_expired`). An owner veto inside the window and a mid-drip halt are the *same write with different reasons* — a veto is "halt at zero sends" — and a second halt is a no-op. It cancels outreach rows in `rendered`/`queued` and **never `sending`**: halt means "no further sends," not "undo," and the residual exposure is one child's send-transaction duration, the same honest contract the Reply lane's veto already has. It never terminalizes the parent directly; it calls `closeBatchIfSettled` like any other terminal writer, so parent terminalization keeps one owner. **There is no resume, and it is structurally prevented** — `halted_at` is monotone, the releaser predicate requires `halted_at IS NULL`, and cancelled outreach rows are terminal; to contact those people the owner builds a new batch. _Avoid_: pause, stop, cancel batch, resume. *(coined in #619 D10; ADR 0014)*
    69	- **Attested postal address**: the owner-attested `businesses.solicitation_postal_address` plus its attestation quartet (`_attested_at`, `_attested_by_user_id`, `_attestation_version`, `_attested_digest`) — the CAN-SPAM §7704(a)(5) sender address baked **verbatim** into every ask footer, and a send precondition. Deliberately **not** `google_place_address`, which is Google's `formattedAddress`: it can be a service-area value like `"Austin, TX, USA"`, is not owner-attested, cannot express a USPS-registered PO box, and is NULLed by the offboarding purge (spec §7.5). Address and attestation are **all-or-nothing by DB CHECK**, and the attestation is welded to the address's **current bytes** by a second CHECK over `_attested_digest` — so no code path can read an unattested address as attested, and no writer can change the stored bytes without recomputing that digest. That guarantee is **narrower than "the attestation is always current"**, and the narrow statement is the load-bearing one: the digest CHECK proves the digest matches the CURRENT address, not that the preserved `_attested_at` / `_attested_by_user_id` / `_attestation_version` ever covered those bytes — a writer that changes the address AND recomputes the digest while keeping the old metadata still passes. Closing that residual needs `OLD` vs `NEW`, which a CHECK cannot see; the trigger was declined by owner decision (2026-08-04, plan "Design decisions" #1). The accidental path — a future `UPDATE … SET solicitation_postal_address = $1` that forgets the attestation — is closed; the residual is forgery rather than oversight. `_attested_by_user_id` is a **plain UUID with no FK** — a point-in-time capture, per migration 093's written lesson that 086's `ON DELETE CASCADE` meant deleting a staff member deleted their uploads. Because there is no FK, the *writer* verifies the actor. _Avoid_: business address, mailing address, footer address. *(coined in #656 — migration 099; owned by `src/lib/solicitation/postal-address.ts`)*
    70	- **Send handoff**: the `enqueueGenerateSolicitationAsks` call at the end of `constructBatch` in `src/lib/solicitation/batch-builder.ts` — the single point where a **Solicitation batch** becomes send-mode work. It is **withheld** — not the batch, and not the individual **Asks** — when the location has no **Attested postal address** or `owner_email_bounced` is TRUE. This is why a missing address is not a **Withhold reason**: it is one per-location fact, not one decision per candidate. The precedence is first-match with `postal_address_missing` ahead of `owner_email_bounced` (it is the CAN-SPAM one), owned by `sendHandoffWithheldReason`. Spec §7.6 point 1 says "no batch produced"; that predates the shared watch/send builder and is **overridden** by §B13 of `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-28-send-mode-cross-spec-amendments.md` — the batch still builds, the **Spoilage report** is unchanged, and only the handoff is withheld. _Avoid_: send gate, generation gate, dispatch gate (that last is #630's, a different thing). *(coined in #656)*
