    82	## Competitor Delta (locked 2026-07-23 — ticket #532, wayfinder map #528)
    83	
    84	- **Competitor Delta line**: the per-location weekly Insights digest line reporting the Named rival's review velocity since the most recent preceding matching snapshot and the review-count gap ("Joe's gained 4 reviews since our last check; gap now 27"), computed from that location's primary tracked keyword's local-pack snapshot. The "since our last check" interval is deliberate because Ranking tracking currently runs biweekly; it must not be described as "this week." Gap = rival's review count minus ours — never rating or rank in v1. Empty states degrade in order: never-configured → line omitted; watching-but-no-snapshot-yet → one teaser line; no preceding match → gap without velocity. *(coined in #532; cadence wording sharpened in #539)*
    85	- **Named rival**: the single local-pack competitor the Competitor Delta line reports on — the owner's pick where one exists, otherwise the Auto-default rival. A pick survives the rival's absence from the pack: an absent pick reports the dropout ("dropped out of the local pack") while the absence spans the latest snapshot window — so the note repeats across weekly digests that read the same biweekly window — then the line falls back to the Auto-default rival until the pick reappears; a pick is never auto-removed. Mechanics: the pick is stored per location as `businesses.rival_place_id` + `rival_title_snapshot`; the live pack title wins whenever the pick is present (a renamed rival reports its current name), and the stored snapshot is only used to name the dropout. Dropout is derived, never stored — a pick absent from the latest pack but present in the immediately preceding one, read from the same two-snapshot window that drives velocity; a pick present with a NULL review count is not a dropout (it fell back, nothing left), and a pack recorded empty for the latest date never raises one. *(coined in #532; pick mechanics locked in #546)*
    86	- **Auto-default rival**: the deterministic stand-in Named rival before any owner pick — the nearest-ahead-by-reviews competitor (smallest positive review-count gap in the latest pack; the nearest challenger tied or behind when no competitor is ahead), ties broken by rank position (NULL last) then place identity. Digest copy labels it `Auto-selected rival` so an algorithmic stand-in is never presented as the owner's choice. An owner replacing it with an explicit pick is itself probe engagement signal. *(coined in #532; disclosure sharpened in #539)*
    87	- **Competitor pack**: the full ~20-entry `local_results` set persisted as `competitor_snapshots` rows per (business, keyword, search_location, snapshot_date) — is_self row included when the location appears, entries with missing place_id/rating/review_count kept with NULLs. Replaced atomically on re-run (replace-pack idempotency); an empty pack for a date is itself a recorded fact. *(coined in #538 grilling)*
