31-- **Live-ingest cutoff**: `connected_at − ZERNIO_RECENT_REVIEW_CONNECT_GRACE_MS` (default 5 min) for a location's active `zernio_connections` row — the instant from which the live lane owns review handling. One owner: `liveIngestCutoff` (`worker/jobs/zernio/zernio-ingest-shared.ts`), consumed by the recent poller (`isRecentForConnection`, ≥ cutoff) and the Review import (Import window upper bound, < cutoff). Null `connected_at` → null cutoff; each lane interprets null per its own fail direction (poller: owns nothing; import: no upper bound). _Avoid_: recency cutoff, connect grace (that names the env var, not the boundary). *(coined in #675 grilling)*
32-- **Reviews list**: the owner's single inventory of every review for a location — the surface the consented Review import lands on. It is **not a new page**: `dashboard/reviews/history` (the former Past Replies archive) is widened in place to include never-replied reviews and becomes it (#671, 2026-08-08; spec §6.3a S1). Grouped `Unanswered` then `Answered` per D6, newest-first inside each group, `PAGE_SIZE` 50. Distinct from the **Needs Action** queue at `dashboard/reviews`, which survives unchanged and answers a different question: that surface filters to `pending_approval` + live auto-post veto windows off the Redis-cached dashboard payload (`ReviewFeedCard.tsx:59-66`, `LIMIT 10`) and can never show an imported review. A review with a pending draft appears in **both** — in the list as a `Draft ready` cross-link with no `Generate` button. Per-row actions split by risk: `Generate` (never-replied) expands the row inline (`InlineGeneratePanel`), `Regenerate` (already-replied) opens the `EditReplyDrawer` two-pane comparison because publishing there **replaces** the owner's live Google reply (spec §6.4). As built (#727), every affordance derives from two orthogonal axes modelled server-side (ADR 0018; replaces #678's six-valued `row_state` precedence chain `recover → regenerate → held → draft_ready → generating → generate`): the **Posted-reply axis** (`reply_state`: `none` / `posted` / `orphan`) — what exists on Google for the review; owns the Unanswered/Answered grouping and the reply panel — and the server-internal **Replacement-draft axis** (`draft_state`: `none` / `generating` / `ready` / `held`, intra-axis precedence held > ready > generating > none), which **never crosses the wire**. The card receives only `reply_state` plus the **Action slot** (`row_action`: `generate` / `generating` / `draft_ready` / `regenerate` / `recover` / `none`) — the single affordance derived from the full 3×4 cross-product (`deriveAxes` + `deriveRowAction`, `src/lib/past-replies/replies-view.ts`). A held draft never projects an affordance of its own (invariant #4 as structure): `none`×held and `posted`×held project `row_action 'none'` — a posted row keeps its live Google reply visible and silently withdraws Regenerate — while `orphan`×held keeps `recover`, because recovery addresses the orphan incident, not the draft. The `held` value itself never reaches the browser: the card reconstructs the "Reply on hold" panel for an unanswered held row from `reply_state 'none'` + `row_action 'none'`. The `gap` / `historical` section split derived from `subscription_activated_at` is deleted here, surviving only as a per-row `ProvenanceBadge` (`posted_before_joining` / `replied_on_google` / `auto_approved` / `owner_approved`); `PAST_REPLIES_VIEW_ENABLED` was **retired with it at #678** — the list renders unconditionally — while `EDIT_REPLIES_ENABLED` is kept (it gates the live-Google mutation) and `editRepliesEnabled()` (`src/lib/past-replies/flags.ts`) is now its only reader. _Avoid_: Past Replies, the archive, History tab (all name the pre-#671 surface), All Reviews page (it is a tab, not a page). *(coined in #671; spec §6.3a, §6.4; implemented at #678; remodelled at #727 per #723)*
33-- **On-demand generation**: owner-initiated LLM drafting from the **Reviews list** — `Generate` on a never-replied review, `Regenerate` on an already-replied one — as opposed to the live-ingest lane, which drafts automatically on every newly ingested review. It is an **owner-controlled LLM spend surface**, governed by four already-existing layers, not by new machinery (#672, 2026-08-08; spec §6.3b): a per-owner-account **rate** limit (`dashregen:owner:{acct}:burst` 10/60s + `:hour` 30/hr, **fails open**), a per-review daily cap (`regen:{reviewId}:{date}`, 3/day — advisory peek at the route, authoritative Lua INCR in `generate-draft.ts:109`, terminal), and the per-business/global **spend** reservation (`cost:daily:{bizId}:{date}`, `cost:global:{date}`). The per-account axis is denominated in **cents, not clicks**. The first `Generate` on a review is **free by construction** — `generate-draft.ts:106` charges only `version > 1`, so the sequence is one free draft then three charged regenerations per review per day; the guard stays because it is what stops the live lane's own auto-draft from eating the owner's regen budget. All three doors share **one** counter, so alternating `Generate` and `Regenerate` cannot double throughput. Because the spend ceiling is shared with the live lane and exhausting it **terminally drops** a draft, `DAILY_COST_LIMIT_CENTS_*` carries a sizing constraint rather than a reserved floor (C4). As built at #678 the two doors are `POST /api/dashboard/reviews/[reviewId]/generate` (never-replied; `origin_lane='on_demand_generate'`, always owner-only — never auto-approved) and the pre-existing `/api/dashboard/past-replies/draft` Regenerate lane, with `GET /api/dashboard/reviews/[reviewId]/draft-status` polling by `reviewId`; a moderation-held response returns `{ status: 'idle' }` and never its text. _Avoid_: on-demand drafting, manual generation, the regenerate budget (that names one layer, not the policy). *(coined in #672; spec §6.3b; implemente