.claude/reference/env-vars.md:40:| `DB_POOL_MAX` | Optional, code default `10`. Postgres.js per-process ceiling on the SHARED write client `sql` (`src/lib/db/server.ts`), env-tunable via `readPoolMax()`. **Set `20` on the Railway worker (staging + prod); set `3` on Vercel** (prod + staging Custom Env + preview); code default stays `10` for anything unset. **Why 20 on the worker:** the hot-four BullMQ workers all contend for this one pool, and their summed concurrency = ingest 5 + generate 5 + notif 4 + publish 4 = **18** (`worker/index.ts` ~194–236), above the old `max:10` — so under the #474 design burst the pool would queue reservations. (18 is worker *concurrency*, NOT 18 held backend connections: a job holds a connection only while its transaction is active, so steady-state demand is lower and bursty.) `20` covers the hot-four + ~2 poller headroom; the `HealthAlertPoller` is already off this pool on its own dedicated `max:2` client, so it does not draw here. `20` is a **ceiling-aware STARTING value blessed only by the staging burst-drill gate** (ADR 0009), bounded above by the measured 60-conn / 57-usable backend ceiling — raise it only with a drill + `pg_stat_activity` evidence, never blind. **Why 3 on Vercel:** each serverless isolate stays small against the Supavisor Max-Clients budget (see note below). The other pool bounds (`idle_timeout: 30`, `max_lifetime: 1800`, `connect_timeout: 10` — Postgres.js takes seconds; `statement_timeout: 30_000` ms) are fixed in code, deep-scan §3.5. |
.claude/reference/env-vars.md-41-| `DB_READ_POOL_MAX` | Optional, default `8`. Postgres.js ceiling on the dedicated **read** client `sqlRead` (`src/lib/db/server.ts`) — the Vercel-side read bulkhead that hosts ONLY `GET /api/dashboard/kpis` (≤6 concurrent) + `GET /api/dashboard/past-replies/draft-status` (≤2 concurrent), so their `Promise.all` waves run one-connection-per-query (the proven #505 non-wedge shape). **Validated + CLAMPED to the reviewed range `[WEDGE_SAFE_READ_MIN = 8, READ_POOL_MAX_CEILING = 8]`** (`readReadPoolMax()`): a value below 8 cannot reintroduce the #505 fan-out wedge (a fan-out > open connections wedges PERMANENTLY in `ClientRead` on the Supavisor transaction pooler), and a value **above** the ceiling cannot silently multiply client connections across Vercel isolates and blow the ADR-0009 ≤16-warm-isolate budget (both clients share the same 57-conn backend). Both bounds are 8 today → the effective read max is **8**; an out-of-range env is clamped to 8 **and warn-logged** (not silently honored). Raising the read pool is a deliberate capacity change: bump `READ_POOL_MAX_CEILING` in `server.ts` AND re-run the ADR-0009 staging burst-drill to re-derive the budget. Read directly via `process.env` in `server.ts`; also declared in the `src/lib/config/server.ts` schema for inventory parity (the config value is not the runtime source — the clamp in `server.ts` is). Tighter 8s read `statement_timeout`. Isolation is LOCAL write-slots only, NOT backend capacity — `sqlRead` shares the same `DATABASE_POOL_URL` / user / db / transaction-mode as `sql`, so it draws from the SAME Supavisor backend pool (ADR 0009). |
