   291	
   292	## D10 — amendment #2: a second, non-fragment-aware `sql` mock asserts on dashboard SQL text
   293	
   294	**When:** step 5, first full verify-gate run. The ONLY red row in an otherwise
   295	23/24 green gate.
   296	
   297	**What the plan assumed:** that the fragment-aware `createMockSql` harness
   298	(`worker/__tests__/helpers/mock-sql.ts`) is how dashboard SQL text gets asserted, so
   299	composing a fragment is invisible to existing tests as long as the shape suites are updated.
   300	
   301	**What actually happened:** `src/app/api/dashboard/__tests__/route.test.ts` defines its **own**
   302	inline `vi.mock('@/lib/db/server', …)` proxy. It renders every interpolation as `?` and returns a
   303	nested fragment as an inert `{ fragmentText, values }` object rather than flattening it into the
   304	parent text. So once the rating-breakdown query composed `reviewTimeWindowFilter`, its captured
   305	text became `AND ?` and the pre-existing assertion
   306	`expect(breakdownSql).toContain('make_interval(days => ?)')` (line 493) failed.
   307	
   308	**Not a production defect.** The SQL is correct and proven three independent ways: the live-DB
   309	suite (13/13 against real Postgres), the fragment-aware shape pins (exact anchor counts), and
   310	`service.rating-breakdown.test.ts` — which asserts the *same string* and passes, because its
   311	harness flattens fragments.
   312	
   313	**Amendment:** added `src/app/api/dashboard/__tests__/route.test.ts` to `allowed_edit_surface` in
   314	both intake copies. **This is amendment #2 of 2** — the abort criteria's trigger — so it was
   315	surfaced to the owner as a stop-and-decide rather than applied unilaterally. Owner granted it,
   316	choosing the minimal one-assertion fix over refactoring that file's mock.
   317	
   318	**What was done:** the assertion now reads through the captured fragment object — one level down —
   319	so BOTH halves of the #403 claim survive rather than being traded away: `make_interval(days => ?)`
   320	is asserted against the fragment's own `fragmentText` (plus a negative check that no
   321	`INTERVAL '<n> days'` literal appears), and `30` is asserted against its flattened bound values.
   322	The net assertion is *stronger* than the original, which only checked the text.
   323	
   324	**Lesson:** the repo has **two** SQL mocks with different fidelity. The shared `createMockSql`
   325	harness flattens nested fragments; the bespoke proxy in the dashboard route test does not. Any
   326	change that pushes SQL text down into a composed fragment is invisible to the first and breaking
   327	to the second. Before composing a fragment into an existing query, grep for every test asserting on
   328	that query's text, not just the ones using the shared harness.
   329	
   330	**Verdict:** ACCEPT — owner-approved, one assertion, no production change, and the invariant it
   331	guards is now better covered than before.

