docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-27-wave-3-pr5b-kpi.md:5:**Goal:** Add a scoped, tested backend KPI layer (`src/lib/kpi/*`) that computes the launch KPI set — response rate, average star rating, review volume MoM, average time-to-respond, and weekly sentiment trend — per-location and aggregated across an account's active locations, plus a read-only `GET /api/dashboard/kpis` data path and PostHog dashboard docs. Visible dashboard cards are a deferred follow-up.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-27-wave-3-pr5b-kpi.md:7:**Architecture:** A new `src/lib/kpi/` module mirrors the existing `dashboard/service.ts` query style (Postgres.js, `Promise.all` of focused scoped queries) but introduces a dedicated `DashboardKpiSummary` type rather than overloading the lifetime `valueSummary`. Per-location queries filter `business_id = $id`; account-aggregate queries `JOIN businesses ... WHERE account_id = $id AND archived_at IS NULL` (the established aggregate-rate pattern). A thin route resolves owner scope exactly like `/api/dashboard` and returns the summary. No migration (the sentiment-trend query is covered by the existing `idx_reviews_business_review_date`).
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-27-wave-3-pr5b-kpi.md:9:**Tech Stack:** TypeScript (ESM, strict), Postgres.js, Next.js route handler, Vitest. Launch-critical slice of Spec 11's KPI section. Stacked on `wave-3-pr5a-sentiment` (reads `reviews.sentiment_score` from migration 052).
