docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-10-feat-688-kpi-review-time-anchor.md:194:- **Review-time anchor**: `LEAST(review_date, detected_at)` — the timestamp the reputation KPIs (review volume MoM, 8-week sentiment trend, avg star) bucket on, so a consented Review import lands in its true months/weeks instead of spiking the import month (and instantly yields a real historical trend). LEAST ignores NULLs: a NULL `review_date` falls back to `detected_at`; a clock-skewed future `review_date` clamps to `detected_at` (unclamped it vanishes from the trend's `generate_series` LEFT JOIN). Workflow surfaces — response rate and the MonthlyImpactWorker digest — deliberately stay on `detected_at`: an import is account activity, and imported unanswered reviews are meant to drag the rate (#675 nudge reasoning). Time-to-respond carries the companion validity filter `approved_at >= detected_at`, so a pre-existing Google reply imported by reconcile can never contribute a negative duration. One owner: `reviewTimeAnchor` (`src/lib/kpi/service.ts`). _Avoid_: review_date anchor (names the column, not the clamp), import exclusion (rejected design — imported rows participate, in their true buckets). *(coined at #688 grilling 2026-08-10; ADR 0019)*
