   748	Only add events that implementation actually emits. Do not add speculative event
   749	names without marking them `planned`.
   750	
   751	#### Customer KPI Reconciliation
   752	
   753	Do not rebuild the dashboard. Extend the existing KPI path.
   754	
   755	Current UI shows:
   756	
   757	- reviews handled
   758	- time saved
   759	- response rate
   760	- pending approvals
   761	
   762	Wave 3 should define and implement the launch KPI set:
   763	
   764	| KPI | Definition | Scope |
   765	|---|---|---|
   766	| Response rate | handled responses divided by received reviews | account/location, last 30 days |
   767	| Average star rating | average `reviews.star_rating` | account/location, last 30 days |
   768	| Review volume MoM | current calendar month vs prior calendar month | account/location |
   769	| Average time-to-respond | average `responses.posted_at` or handled timestamp minus review date | account/location, last 30 days |
   770	| Sentiment trend | weekly average sentiment score and trend | account/location, last 8 weeks |
   771	
   772	Because current `valueSummary` uses lifetime-style value metrics, introduce a
   773	new focused type such as `DashboardKpiSummary` rather than overloading the
   774	existing value summary.
   775	
   776	Query rules:
   777	
   778	- Scope every query by `account_id` and, when selected, `business_id`.
   779	- No new repository layer. Use focused modules such as `src/lib/kpi/*` or
   780	  colocated dashboard query modules.
   781	- Keep aggregate "all locations" behavior explicit.
   782	- Add tests for account scoping, location scoping, and archived-location
   783	  exclusion.
   784	
   785	#### Sentiment Classification
   786	
   787	Add sentiment fields on `reviews`:
   788	
   789	- `sentiment_score numeric`
   790	- `sentiment_label text`
   791	- `sentiment_classified_at timestamptz`
   792	- optional `sentiment_source text`
   793	
   794	Labels:
   795	
   796	- `positive`
   797	- `neutral`
   798	- `negative`
   799	
