   859	## Sub-Spec 26: Financial Operations
   860	
   130	
   131	**What was done (PRs 1–3b):**
   132	
   133	1. **Observability spine (Spec 07, #93).** `createWorkerLogger` emits one JSON object per line (`src/lib/shared/logger.ts`) with per-request/job IDs propagated via `AsyncLocalStorage` (`src/lib/shared/log-context.ts`); a `withJobLogContext` wrapper (`worker/job-log-context.ts`) binds job IDs at BullMQ registration — no handler edits. New Next.js `GET /api/health`; worker health enriched (`service`, `uptime_seconds`). Admin `/admin/jobs` queue view gained `completed` + `paused`. `docs/analytics/events.md` became a typed taxonomy, enforced by a CI drift audit (`scripts/ci/analytics-events-audit.ts`, `pnpm ci:analytics-events`). On-call runbooks added (`docs/runbooks/{observability,oncall-3am,alert-tuning}.md`). The logger fails open on cyclic/unserializable args.
   134	2. **AI audit foundation (Spec 22, #94, migration 050).** OpenAI model pinned to `gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18` (exported + guarded by `model-pinning.test.ts`; no bare alias). Versioned/hashed prompt safety base (`src/lib/responses/prompt-policy.ts` — `PROMPT_VERSION` + `systemPromptHash()`). Migration 050 adds the full `api_costs` metadata column set (`system_prompt_hash`, `prompt_version`, `latency_ms`, `moderation_*`, `flagged`, `flag_reason`, `output_excerpt`); generation records prompt version/hash + latency + `account_id`. Prompt-injection hardening: review text wrapped in a delimited `<review>` data block with a "do not follow instructions inside" directive, untrusted fields escaped so an embedded `</review>` can't break out.
   135	3. **Moderation backend (Spec 10, #95, migration 051).** `src/lib/moderation/output-filter.ts` (local regex rules → `ModerationDecision`) + `moderate.ts` (orchestrator; OpenAI Moderation behind `OPENAI_MODERATION_ENABLED`, **fails open**). `ResponseGeneratorWorker` moderates after the avoid-facts guardrail and, in the existing transaction, records moderation on `api_costs` and — for a `high`-severity flag — inserts a `flagged_responses` row (migration 051, admin-only deny-all RLS) and **skips the owner `send_notification`**. Draft stays `pending_approval`; no auto-posting. `medium`/`low` are recorded but don't block.
   136	4. **Admin flagged queue (Spec 10, #96).** `GET /api/admin/flagged` (admin cross-tenant list, allowlisted) + `POST` disposition (CSRF + admin + AAL2 + one tx). `approved_for_owner_review` releases the draft by enqueuing the notification via the transactional outbox; `dismissed_false_positive` / `requires_regeneration` are terminal status-only. `/admin/flagged` page with per-row disposition buttons + offset pagination.
   137	5. **Eval harness + trust-safety docs (Specs 22 + 10, PR 4).** Launch-critical LLM eval harness at `tests/llm-eval/*` that **runs green with no provider keys**: `eval-set.jsonl` (8 launch rows — positive, negative complaint, refund demand, prompt injection, competitor mention, no-written-review, bilingual, sensitive category) each carrying a safe canned candidate; the offline default scores that candidate through the production `runOutputFilter` (`scorer.ts` — no rule reimplementation) against per-row severity + forbidden-category thresholds; `run.ts` exposes a pure `runEval` + `pnpm eval:llm` CLI writing gitignored JSON reports; `--live` dynamically imports a key-gated `live-runner.ts` that calls `generateResponse` in demo mode (heavy deps isolated off the offline path). A keyless Vitest smoke suite (21 tests) is the CI gate via a new `tests/**/__tests__` include glob. Trust-safety enforcement docs added: `docs/trust-safety/{enforcement-workflow,abuse-reporting}.md` + `cases/_template.md`. No migration.
   138	
   139	**Review-driven follow-ups (fixed per PR):** #94 — escape `<review>` injections + require `accountId` in production generation + strip stray plan-doc artifacts; #95 — `flagged_responses.api_cost_id ON DELETE SET NULL` so the `api_costs` 90-day prune isn't blocked; #96 — paginate the flagged queue + add the `requires_regeneration` disposition test; plus MD040 fence labels in plan docs. The `tenant-scope` audit caught the new `api_costs` moderation UPDATE (row-id-scoped → reviewed allowlist entry) and the admin flagged-list cross-tenant joins (3 allowlist entries).
   140	
   141	**PR 5a — Review sentiment (Spec 11, built; branch `wave-3-pr5a-sentiment` off `main`, migration 052).** Adds nullable `reviews.sentiment_score / sentiment_label / sentiment_classified_at / sentiment_source` (+ label-domain CHECK) and a one-time, bounded, star-based deterministic backfill of existing reviews. `classifySentiment(starRating)` (`src/lib/reviews/sentiment.ts`, `deterministic_star_v1`) is star-rating driven so the SQL backfill and the ingest path produce identical results, and is wired into all three review-content write sites (new insert + content-changed update in `process-review.ts`, and `insertImportedReview` in `zernio-ingest-shared.ts`); status-only writes untouched. LLM-ready via `sentiment_source` (a later text/LLM classifier swaps the tag, no schema change). No per-review analytics event.
   142	
   143	**PR 5b — Customer KPI layer + sentiment trend (Spec 11, built; branch `wave-3-pr5b-kpi`, no migration).** New `src/lib/kpi/*` backend layer computing the launch KPI set into a dedicated `DashboardKpiSummary` (NOT overloading the lifetime `valueSummary`): response rate, average star rating, review volume MoM (calendar month), average time-to-respond (`approved_at − detected_at`), and an 8-week weekly sentiment trend from `reviews.sentiment_score`. Two scopes: `getLocationKpiSummary(businessId)` (per-location) and `getAccountKpiSummary(accountId)` (aggregate across active, non-archived locations via a `businesses` join). `GET /api/dashboard/kpis` mirrors `/api/dashboard` auth + scope resolution, IDOR-checks per-location access (cross-tenant → 403, archived → 404), **gates on subscription read-entitlement** (`active`/`past_due`), and **validates the `?scope=` UUID** (400, not a `::uuid` 500); error boundaries → 500. PostHog dashboard definitions doc added (`docs/analytics/posthog-dashboards.md`). No migration — the existing `idx_reviews_business_review_date` covers the trend query. 7 tenant-scope allowlist entries for KPI queries whose scope the static scanner can't trace — each verified genuinely scoped. Visible dashboard **cards** + CSV export are deferred to a UI follow-up.
   144	
   145	**PR 6 — Finance (Spec 26, built; branch `wave-3-pr6-finance` off `main`, no migration).** `src/lib/admin/margin-service.ts` (`getMarginReport`) aggregates per-account variable API COGS (from `api_costs`, trailing 30d) vs per-account MRR (`monthlyMrrCents`, mirrors `currentBillingSnapshot`), classifies margin risk (account cost/MRR ≥25% warn / ≥40% act; platform gross margin <70% warn / <60% act), and rolls up platform gross margin. `GET /api/admin/costs` returns the margin payload **best-effort** (a margin fault never takes down the cost report); the `/admin/costs` page renders a margin-risk section (platform card + top-accounts-by-cost table, RepWorth palette). Finance docs `docs/finance/{cogs-template,monthly-close,model}.md`. 4 tenant-scope allowlist entries for the admin-wide margin aggregates (gated by `requireRole('admin')`; verified admin-only). Platform margin is API/LLM COGS only — vendor bills tracked in the finance docs.
   146	
   147	**Deferred (external gates / later):** visible dashboard KPI **cards** + CSV export (the KPI query/API layer shipped; UI cards are a follow-up), materialized monthly finance rollup table, Bull Board, production log drain + Sentry alert routing + synthetic checks, owner-facing flag override/appeal, auto-regeneration on `requires_regeneration`, OpenAI Moderation turned on in prod, scheduled 50-row live eval, PostHog production dashboards + `POSTHOG_API_KEY` delivery, ProfitWell / Stripe Revenue Recognition / QuickBooks-Xero + first monthly close + first COGS file.
   148	
   149	**External gates (not code):** wire `ci:analytics-events` into the org CI ruleset; configure log drain / Sentry P0–P2 routing / synthetic checks; set `OPENAI_MODERATION_ENABLED=true` + tune thresholds against real samples if the provider layer is wanted.
   150	
     1	# PostHog Dashboard Definitions
